build 10: VOICE all the way down with MUSICAL on now keeps the natural sound of your voice for big jumps too (up to an octave), not just small ones, and the last little clicks it could leave are gone. DRAG MIDI now carries the chords as a second track (named CHORDS, channel 2): the CHORD BED's notes when it is on, otherwise the take's chords. Older takes you edit keep their own sound: the same syllables and, for CHOPS, the same chops in the same phrase. Version 1.6.2. build 9: VOICE all the way down with MUSICAL on now sounds much closer to your real recording: small re-pitches (up to a fifth) move your voice's own periods in order and keep its vowels exactly, instead of rebuilding it. A new CHORD BED slider on PLAY IT (INSTRUMENT) holds the take's chords softly under the melody on the same voice, so RICH chords and chord swaps can be heard (off by default). Older takes can be edited straight away (they upgrade themselves; undo brings the old one back). VARY remembers notes you deleted. A chop note you move to another octave really plays in that octave. TEXTURE edits re-render in a fraction of a second like the others. Version 1.6.1. build 8: UNDER THE HOOD's MELODY roll is yours to edit. Drag notes up and down (they only land on notes of the key, so nothing can go out of key) and left and right (onto the GRID: 1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32), drag a note's right end to make it longer, double-click to add a note, double-click or DELETE to remove one, drag on empty space to select several, arrow keys move them, UNDO / REDO / RESET NOTES. The take re-renders in about half a second, your notes are saved with the session, VARY keeps them and DRAG MIDI exports them. A new PLAY IT tab has ArpEZator's controls: MASTER (simple to wild), CHORDS (AS WRITTEN / SIMPLE / RICH), the ARP (FIGURE, UP, DOWN, UP-DOWN, RANDOM, PENDULUM, CONVERGE, RATE 1/8 or 1/16, 1-3 OCTAVES) and the line between two notes (STEP, GLIDE, FATTEN). Click any chord name under the roll to swap it for another chord in the key; the melody follows. POP BRAIN and ACID BRAIN are now called LEARNED POP and LEARNED ACID. Version 1.6.0. build 7: a new style group, PARLOUR PIANO, with two moods - WISTFUL (an old-fashioned parlour piano: slow, gentle chords, a swaying left hand, a floating tune) and STILL NIGHT (slower and sparser, long held notes). It plays from a small model learned from 12 old piano scores; every take is new. Version 1.5.1. build 6: a much more beautiful sound. VOICE (the new knob next to TONE and SPACE for INSTRUMENT): all the way down plays your real recording, its actual words in the melody's timing; turn it up and the voice turns smoothly into a clean, soft instrument made from it (no buzz, no distortion). PAD gets DREAM (longer, glassier, dreamier, with a soft octave shimmer), TEXTURE gets DRIFT and CHOPS gets STUTTER. A STYLE browser with every melody style we have made (Block Step and Ghost House piano and synth styles, REVERIE, the learned POP and ACID brains, ArpEZator's arps, hooks, trap and hip hop) - click one to hear it - plus < > and LENGTH (1 to 16 bars). UNDER THE HOOD shows what each take type is doing, step by step, with its deeper knobs. VARY now makes a clear variation of the same idea. Version 1.5.0. build 5: the highlighted parts on the waveform are yours to edit, like slices in a sampler: drag a box to move it, drag its edges to resize it (they snap to zero crossings and to where syllables start; hold Shift to place freely), and the take rebuilds from your parts while the old one keeps playing. Double-click to add a part (a new chop), right-click for Delete / Split / Duplicate / Hear, Alt-drag copies, a click plays that part (and flashes its key for CHOPS), Cmd+Z undoes each edit. VARY keeps your parts, GENERATE starts fresh, and your parts are saved with the project. Version 1.4.0. build 4: a CLEAR switch (the small pill next to CHARACTER, on for new takes) that keeps your sound clean and true: a real sample on every key instead of one every few keys, a steady pitch with no wobble, chorus or detuned double, no warmth grit or limiter squash, cleaner PAD and TEXTURE grains over the voice itself, and CHOPS that play your original audio untouched when they are already in tune. Turn it off for the dreamier, blurrier sound; older projects open with it off so they sound the same. Version 1.3.0. build 3: the installer removes the old Ghost Slice the collection installer left in /Library (it was loading instead of the new one), version 1.2.0 so FL and Logic rescan. build 2: the new window exactly like the reference picture (deep indigo, violet -> cyan glow, Poppins font): glass panels, TAKE TYPE / CHARACTER tiles, waveform zoom + overview + TRIM + play the sound, take cards with mini waveforms, VELOCITY meter, SCALE box with key lock; INPUT moved into the gear menu
